        "original_id": "86509b25-068a-5b20-9d81-c57dcd60eb31",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alberic II of Spoleto, Marozia, Pope Leo VII, King Hugh of Italy, Pope Sergius III, Pope John X\n- Places: Rome, Italy\n- Roles: ruler of Rome, Roman noblewoman, pope\n\nFacts:\n- Marozia, born Maria and also known as Mariuccia or Mariozza, lived from about 890 to 937.\n- Marozia was a Roman noblewoman, was the alleged mistress of Pope Sergius III, and received the unprecedented titles \"senatrix\" and \"patricia\" of Rome from Pope John X.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto lived from 912 to 954.\n- In 932, Alberic II of Spoleto became ruler of Rome after deposing his mother Marozia and his stepfather, King Hugh of Italy.\n- Alberic II of Spoleto ruled Rome from 932 to 954.\n- Pope Leo VII's election to the papacy was secured by Alberic II of Spoleto, who was the ruler of Rome at that time.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
